'' 'extern import' IS A DLL'S VARIABLE, AND IS LOADED THROUGH ITS IMPORT POINTER (T85). The
'' keyword was consumed and dropped, so the variable was referenced directly, and an import
'' library defines only '__imp_<name>' for data: against a clang-built DLL exporting
'' 'int MyDll_Data', 'lld-link: error: undefined symbol: MyDll_Data'. Emitted 'dllimport'
'' now, it reads &h1234, and a write and an '@' go through the DLL's own storage (measured
'' 2026-10-03). A plain 'extern' is unchanged. See src/codegen/llvmglobal.bas.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --emit-ir -target windows-x86_64 tests/codegen/src/extern-import.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: @"MyDll_Data" = external dllimport global i32
'' EXPECT-OUT: @"Plain_Data" = external global i32
